# What a golden case that is a folder may ask of the run beside its files
# (M-package-manager step 5b): a shape no file of the repository can hold, a
# machine with no git, a program git places in no repository, a link on the
# way to a source, a variable clang or `pkg-config` reads. Three files beside
# `main.hero`, any of them:
#
#     environment    `NAME=VALUE` a line, given to the case's run alone and
#                    never to this process, `<root>` in a value standing for
#                    the repository's root as git answers it
#     links          `<name> <target>` a line, a symbolic link made in the
#                    case before its run, holding `<target>` as written
#     directory      one line, a folder of the case: its run starts there,
#                    so `.` names it for the compiler and every clang it runs
#
# **No link is ever made in the tree**: a case with links runs in a copy under
# the harness's scratch folder (`build/`, inside the repository, so git
# answers the same root there), its links made in the copy with `ln -s` as
# `apply_tree.hero` makes its own, and the case is skipped by name where `ln`
# is not the machine's, Windows. **What a case prints is written back as the
# case's own**: the copy's folder as the case's, absolute and relative, and
# the repository's root as `<root>`, so one expectation holds on every
# machine. A case whose expectation writes `<root>` and asks nothing runs in
# place, its root written back the same way.
#
# **Which variables, a fact about each**: `PATH` and `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`,
# the two whose empty value reads as unset to what a case's compiler runs (an
# empty ceiling list is none to git, and `PATH` is set in every run of this
# harness). Since feature 2424 (panel 242's R6) they are given to the case's
# run at its start (`shell.run_given`), and this process's environment is
# never written; until then they were set here and put back after the run,
# empty where this run had them unset, since the runtime had no unset, and
# that is why only a variable whose empty value reads as unset was admitted.
# The case's compiler is found through this process's `PATH`, never the
# case's, which is its run's alone. **And the three clang reads into every
# compile** (`CLANG_READS`, panel 237's R2, defect 2344): their empty value is
# no unset, Apple clang searching `.` for an empty `CPATH`, so they are never
# set in this harness's own process, where every later case's clang would
# read them. **And the two `pkg-config` reads** (`PKG_CONFIG_READS`, panel
# 243's R2, defect 2428): the compiler starts `pkg-config` for a `pkgconfig`
# group, so a case carries a library of its own, a `.pc` naming its folder by
# `${pcfiledir}` (`prefix=${pcfiledir}/..`) beside the headers it describes,
# with no absolute path, and `PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR` naming the same folder hides
# the machine's, so the case is hermetic. An empty `PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR` is no
# unset either, `pkg-config` then searching no folder at all. Any other name
# is refused with the case's name, never given.
#
# **Every variable reaches the case's run through `shell.run_given`, on every
# platform** (defect 2477), an empty value set empty on Windows too
# (`hero_run_env`); until then the five reads went through `/usr/bin/env`, and
# 24 cases were never judged on Windows. A list of folders is written with
# POSIX's `:` and given with `;` there (`FOLDER_LISTS`), so one `environment`
# holds on every machine, as `<root>` makes one expectation do.
#
# **A case with a `directory` runs from a copy of its folder**, as one with
# links does, since the compiler writes its cache under the folder it runs in:
# started there by `/usr/bin/env -C`, with the compiler and the case's own
# paths written whole, so an empty element of `CPATH` names a folder of the
# case and never the repository's root. The runtime's spawn starts every
# child in this process's folder (`hero_run_go` in `runtime/parts/run.c`
# passes `CreateProcessW` no folder and calls no `chdir`), so no other route
# exists, and such a case is skipped by name on Windows.

use <core>/strings as core_strings

use apply_tree
use shell
use strings
use variables_probe

# The variables a case's `environment` may give its run.
constant SETTABLE: [str]
    ["PATH", "GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES"]

# The variables clang reads into every compile, which a case's `environment`
# may set for its compiler alone.
constant CLANG_READS: [str]
    ["CPATH", "C_INCLUDE_PATH", "CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS"]

# The variables `pkg-config` reads where the compiler asks it for a
# `pkgconfig` group, which a case's `environment` may set for its compiler
# alone, as the clang reads are.
constant PKG_CONFIG_READS: [str]
    ["PKG_CONFIG_PATH", "PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR"]

# The variables whose value is a list of folders, written in a case with
# POSIX's `:` between them and given with `;` on Windows, where a folder holds
# a drive's `:`: LLVM 22.1.8's `llvm/Support/Program.h` gives
# `EnvPathSeparator` as `;` on `_WIN32`, pkgconf 3.0.10's
# `libpkgconf/stdinc.h` gives `PKG_CONFIG_PATH_SEP_S` the same (both read
# on this Mac, 2026-11-12), and the compiler parts the four reads so
# (`cli/clang_added.hero`, `cli/pkgconfig_answer.hero`). `CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS`
# holds edits, never folders.
constant FOLDER_LISTS: [str]
    ["PATH", "GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES", "CPATH", "C_INCLUDE_PATH", "PKG_CONFIG_PATH", "PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR"]

# The one program that starts a case's compiler from a folder of its own,
# which the runtime's spawn cannot: POSIX's `env`, `-C` in GNU's and in this
# Mac's.
constant ENV: str
    "/usr/bin/env"

# What a case asks of its run: each variable `NAME=VALUE`, each link `name
# target`, as written, and the folder it starts in, "" for none.
record Setting
    environment: [str]
    links: [str]
    directory: str

# The setting of the case in the folder `dir`, none where it asks nothing, or
# the refusal of a line it may not write.
function read_setting(dir: str) -> Setting?
    environment = lines_of(read_file(dir + "/environment").default(""))
    links = lines_of(read_file(dir + "/links").default(""))
    directory = lines_of(read_file(dir + "/directory").default(""))

    for pair in environment
        cut = strings.index_of(text: pair, needle: "=")

        if cut.is_err() || !settable(pair.slice(from: 0, to: cut.must())) && !reads(pair.slice(from: 0, to: cut.must()))
            return fail(
                code: "setting",
                msg: dir + "/environment sets `" + pair + "`, and a case sets only " + SETTABLE.join(" and ") + ", the variables whose empty value reads as unset, " + CLANG_READS.join(", ") + ", which clang reads, and " + PKG_CONFIG_READS.join(" and ") + ", which `pkg-config` reads, as `NAME=VALUE`"
            )

    for link in links
        if strings.split_on(text: link, byte: 32).len() != 2
            return fail(code: "setting", msg: dir + "/links holds `" + link + "`, and a link is `<name> <target>`")

    if directory.len() > 1 || directory.len() == 1 && !inside(directory[0])
        return fail(
            code: "setting",
            msg: dir + "/directory holds `" + directory.join(" ") + "`, and it is one line, a folder of the case named from it"
        )
    return ok(Setting(environment: environment, links: links, directory: directory.join("")))

# Whether `path` names a folder inside the case: relative, and never climbing.
function inside(path: str) -> bool
    if path.len() == 0 || path[0] == '/' || path[0] == '\\'
        return false

    for part in strings.split_on(text: path, byte: 47)
        if part == ".."
            return false

    return true

# The code a case skipped here fails with, which a form keeps as a skip.
constant SKIP: str
    "setting_skipped"

# Why the case `s` names cannot run on this machine, "" where it can: a link
# made with `ln`, or a run started in a folder of the case's own by
# `/usr/bin/env -C`, neither of which Windows has. A variable is never a
# reason: every one is given at the spawn, on every platform (defect 2477).
function skip_here(s: Setting) -> str
    if s.links.len() > 0 && shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
        return "the case makes a symbolic link with `ln -s` before its run, as `apply_tree.hero`'s link cases do, and this platform has no `ln`"

    if started_by_env(s) && shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
        return "the case starts its compiler in its folder `" + s.directory + "`, which the runtime's spawn cannot give a child (`hero_run_go` starts every child in this process's folder), so `" + ENV + " -C` starts it, and this platform has no `" + ENV + "`"
    return ""

# Whether the case's compiler is started through `/usr/bin/env`: in a folder
# of its own.
function started_by_env(s: Setting) -> bool
    return s.directory.len() > 0

# Whether a run failed as a case skipped here.
function is_skip(said: shell.Run?) -> bool
    match said
        .ok _  => return false
        .err e => return e.code == SKIP

# Whether a case asks anything of its run.
function asks(s: Setting) -> bool
    return s.environment.len() > 0 || s.links.len() > 0 || s.directory.len() > 0

# Whether `name` is a variable a case may set in this process.
function settable(name: str) -> bool
    for one in SETTABLE
        if one == name
            return true

    return false

# Whether `name` is a variable clang or `pkg-config` reads, set for a case's
# compiler alone.
function reads(name: str) -> bool
    for one in CLANG_READS
        if one == name
            return true

    for one in PKG_CONFIG_READS
        if one == name
            return true

    return false

# The repository's root as git answers it, absolute.
function repository_root(scratch: str) -> str?
    asked = shell.run(scratch: scratch, program: "git", words: ["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"])?

    if asked.code != 0
        return fail(
            code: "no_repository",
            msg: "the case writes `<root>` or asks its run something, and git answers no repository root here: " + asked.err
        )
    return ok(strings.trimmed(asked.out))

# The run of `words` for the case in `dir` as `s` asks it, what it printed
# written back as the case's own: in a copy holding its links or starting in
# its folder, every variable given to its run alone at the spawn, and through
# `/usr/bin/env -C` where it starts in a folder of its own, which hands them
# on.
function ran(scratch: str, program: str, words: [str], dir: str, s: Setting, root: str) -> shell.Run?
    at: str @= dir
    line: [str] @= words

    if s.links.len() > 0 || s.directory.len() > 0
        at @ scratch + "/set/" + strings.base_name(path: dir)
        apply_tree.copy_tree(scratch: scratch, from: dir, to: at)?

        for link in s.links
            parts = strings.split_on(text: link, byte: 32)
            made = shell.run(scratch: scratch, program: "ln", words: ["ln", "-s", parts[1], at + "/" + parts[0]])?

            if made.code != 0
                return fail(
                    code: "setting",
                    msg: "`ln -s " + parts[1] + " " + at + "/" + parts[0] + "` exited " + made.code.to_str() + ": " + made.err
                )

        line @ swapped_all(words: words, old: dir, new: at)
    started: str @= program

    if started_by_env(s)
        line @ env_line(line, directory: s.directory, at: whole(root: root, path: at), root: root)
        started @ ENV
    said = shell.run_given(
        scratch: scratch,
        program: started,
        words: line,
        given: given_all(s: s, root: root, windows: shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe")
    )

    if at != dir
        _ = shell.remove_tree(at).is_err()
    back: shell.Run @= said?
    back.out @ written_back(text: back.out, at: at, dir: dir, root: root)
    back.err @ written_back(text: back.err, at: at, dir: dir, root: root)
    return ok(back)

# **The line that starts a case's compiler in its `directory`** of `at`, its
# copy, through `/usr/bin/env -C`: the compiler and the copy's paths written
# whole, since a relative one would be read from there. The case's variables
# are given to `env` at the spawn, and `env` hands them on.
function env_line(words: [str], directory: str, at: str, root: str) -> [str]
    out: [str] @= [ENV, "-C", at + "/" + directory, whole(root: root, path: words[0])]

    for word in words.slice(from: 1, to: words.len())
        out @ out.push(swapped(text: word, old: unwhole(root: root, path: at), new: at))

    return out

# Every variable the case `s` sets, as its run is given it (`given_value`), in
# the order the case wrote them, so a name written twice takes its later
# value, as `hero_run_env` gives it.
function given_all(s: Setting, root: str, windows: bool) -> [shell.Variable]
    out: [shell.Variable] @= []

    for pair in s.environment
        cut = strings.index_of(text: pair, needle: "=").must()
        name = pair.slice(from: 0, to: cut)
        out @ out.push(
            shell.Variable(name: name, value: given_value(name: name, value: pair.slice(from: cut + 1, to: pair.len()), root: root, windows: windows))
        )

    return out

# The value a case's `NAME=VALUE` gives its run: each `<root>` the
# repository's root, and a list of folders (`FOLDER_LISTS`) parted at the `:`
# the case writes and joined by the platform's `separator`, each part's root
# written after the parting, since a root on Windows holds a drive's `:`. An
# empty part stays one, an empty value stays set and empty.
function given_value(name: str, value: str, root: str, windows: bool) -> str
    if !folder_list(name)
        return swapped(text: value, old: "<root>", new: root)
    out: [str] @= []

    for part in strings.split_on(text: value, byte: 58)
        out @ out.push(swapped(text: part, old: "<root>", new: root))

    return out.join(separator(windows))

# What parts a list of folders a run is given: `;` on Windows, `:` elsewhere.
function separator(windows: bool) -> str
    if windows
        return ";"
    return ":"

# Whether `name`'s value is a list of folders.
function folder_list(name: str) -> bool
    for one in FOLDER_LISTS
        if one == name
            return true

    return false

# `path` written whole: as it is where it starts at the root, else from the
# repository's root.
function whole(root: str, path: str) -> str
    if path.len() > 0 && path[0] == '/'
        return path

    if core_strings.has_prefix(s: path, prefix: "./")
        return root + "/" + path.slice(from: 2, to: path.len())
    return root + "/" + path

# `path`, written whole, as the repository's root reads it.
function unwhole(root: str, path: str) -> str
    return strings.without_prefix(text: path, prefix: root + "/")

# `text` with the folder the case ran in written as the case's own, and the
# repository's root as `<root>`: the absolute form first.
function written_back(text: str, at: str, dir: str, root: str) -> str
    moved: str @= text

    if at != dir
        moved @ swapped(text: moved, old: root + "/" + at, new: "<root>/" + dir)
        moved @ swapped(text: moved, old: at, new: dir)
    return swapped(text: moved, old: root, new: "<root>")

function swapped_all(words: [str], old: str, new: str) -> [str]
    out: [str] @= []

    for word in words
        out @ out.push(swapped(text: word, old: old, new: new))

    return out

# `text` with every `old` written `new`.
function swapped(text: str, old: str, new: str) -> str
    if old.len() == 0
        return text
    return strings.split_text(text: text, separator: old).join(new)

# The lines of a setting's file, blank ones and `#` comments left out.
function lines_of(text: str) -> [str]
    out: [str] @= []

    for one in strings.split_on(text: text, byte: 10)
        line = strings.trimmed(one)

        if line.len() > 0 && line[0] != '#'
            out @ out.push(line)

    return out

## Tests

test "a case's printed folder and root are written back as its own"
    got = written_back(
        text: "build/h-1/set/x.case/main.hero:1:5: error[e]: through `/r/build/h-1/set/x.case/linked`, in `/r`",
        at: "build/h-1/set/x.case",
        dir: "tests/golden/check/x.case",
        root: "/r"
    )
    assert got == "tests/golden/check/x.case/main.hero:1:5: error[e]: through `<root>/tests/golden/check/x.case/linked`, in `<root>`"
    assert written_back(text: "outside `/r`", at: "d", dir: "d", root: "/r") == "outside `<root>`"

test "a setting names only the variables whose empty value reads as unset, and links of two words"
    assert settable("PATH")
    assert settable("GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES")
    assert !settable("GIT_DIR")
    assert !settable("HOME")
    assert lines_of("# why\nPATH=<root>/build/no-tools\n\n") == ["PATH=<root>/build/no-tools"]
    none = Setting(environment: [], links: [], directory: "")
    assert !asks(none)
    assert !started_by_env(none)

# **A variable clang reads is never set in this process** (defect 2344): it
# is given to the case's run alone, at the spawn since defect 2477, a
# `<root>` in its value written whole, so no case starts its compiler through
# `/usr/bin/env` for a variable; and a case with a `directory` starts there
# through `/usr/bin/env -C`, its compiler and its copy's paths written whole,
# so nothing is read from the folder it starts in but what the case meant.
test "a variable clang reads is given to the case's run alone, and a directory is where its run starts"
    assert reads("CPATH") && reads("C_INCLUDE_PATH") && reads("CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS")
    assert !settable("CPATH") && !reads("PATH")
    plain = Setting(environment: ["PATH=/x", "CPATH=<root>/inc"], links: [], directory: "")
    assert !started_by_env(plain)
    given = given_all(s: plain, root: "/r", windows: false)
    assert given.len() == 2 && given[0].name == "PATH" && given[0].value == "/x" && given[1].name == "CPATH" && given[1].value == "/r/inc"
    words = ["./heroes-next", "build", "build/h-1/set/x.case/main.hero"]
    moved = Setting(environment: ["C_INCLUDE_PATH=:"], links: [], directory: "here")
    assert started_by_env(moved)
    assert env_line(words, directory: moved.directory, at: "/r/build/h-1/set/x.case", root: "/r") == [ENV, "-C", "/r/build/h-1/set/x.case/here", "/r/heroes-next", "build", "/r/build/h-1/set/x.case/main.hero"]
    assert inside("here") && inside("a/b") && !inside("../up") && !inside("/abs") && !inside("a/../..")
    assert whole(root: "/r", path: "/abs") == "/abs" && unwhole(root: "/r", path: "/r/b/c") == "b/c"

# **The two `pkg-config` reads go to the case's run alone** (panel 243's R2,
# defect 2428): a case naming its own `.pc` folder sets `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` and
# `PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR`, which reach its run at the spawn in the order the case
# wrote them, never this process's environment, where every later case's
# `pkg-config` would read them; any other variable of `pkg-config`'s is
# refused by name.
test "a case's own pkg-config folder is given to its run alone, and another pkg-config variable is refused (defect 2428)"
    assert reads("PKG_CONFIG_PATH") && reads("PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR")
    assert !settable("PKG_CONFIG_PATH") && !settable("PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR") && !reads("PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR")
    dir = "build/selftest-case-setting-pc"
    assert !shell.remove_tree(dir).is_err()
    assert !shell.mkdir_all(dir).is_err()
    assert !write_file(path: dir + "/environment", text: "# the case's own library\nPKG_CONFIG_PATH=" + dir + "/pc\nPKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR=" + dir + "/pc\n").is_err()
    got = read_setting(dir).must()
    assert !started_by_env(got) && skip_here(got) == ""
    given = given_all(s: got, root: "/r", windows: true)
    assert given.len() == 2 && given[0].name == "PKG_CONFIG_PATH" && given[1].name == "PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR"
    assert given[0].value == dir + "/pc" && given[1].value == dir + "/pc"
    assert !write_file(path: dir + "/environment", text: "PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/x\n").is_err()

    said = match read_setting(dir)
        .ok _  => "ok"
        .err e => e.msg

    assert said == dir + "/environment sets `PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/x`, and a case sets only PATH and GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES, the variables whose empty value reads as unset, CPATH, C_INCLUDE_PATH, CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS, which clang reads, and PKG_CONFIG_PATH and PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR, which `pkg-config` reads, as `NAME=VALUE`"
    assert !shell.remove_tree(dir).is_err()

# **A list of folders a case writes with `:` is given with the platform's
# separator** (defect 2477): `;` on Windows, where a folder holds a drive's
# `:`, so a `<root>` is written after the parting and its own `:` is never a
# cut; an empty part stays one, an empty value stays empty, and an edit of
# `CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS` is never parted. Every variable a case may set is a
# list of folders but that one, so a variable admitted later is classed here.
test "a list of folders a case writes with `:` is given with `;` on Windows, its root written after the parting (defect 2477)"
    assert given_value(name: "PKG_CONFIG_PATH", value: "a/pa:a/pb", root: "/r", windows: false) == "a/pa:a/pb"
    assert given_value(name: "PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR", value: "a/pa:a/pb", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == "a/pa;a/pb"
    assert given_value(name: "CPATH", value: "<root>/inc:x", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == "C:/w/inc;x"
    assert given_value(name: "C_INCLUDE_PATH", value: ":", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == ";"
    assert given_value(name: "C_INCLUDE_PATH", value: "/nonexistent-2344:", root: "/r", windows: false) == "/nonexistent-2344:"
    assert given_value(name: "CPATH", value: "", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == ""
    assert given_value(name: "GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES", value: "<root>", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == "C:/w"
    assert given_value(name: "CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS", value: "#+-D<root>=a:b", root: "C:/w", windows: true) == "#+-DC:/w=a:b"

    for names in [SETTABLE, CLANG_READS, PKG_CONFIG_READS]
        for name in names
            assert folder_list(name) == (name != "CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS")

# **Every variable reaches the case's run at its spawn, on every platform**
# (defect 2477): asked of a program clang builds, which prints what it was
# given, in the compiler's place. A value set empty stays set, a value holding
# a space comes whole, the case's `PATH` takes the place of this process's
# own, a list comes with the platform's separator, and this process holds none
# of them after. A case with a `directory` starts there through `/usr/bin/env
# -C`, which hands its variables on, and on Windows it is skipped by its
# folder's name.
test "a case's variables reach its run at the spawn on every platform, and a directory is where it starts (defect 2477)"
    scratch = "build/selftest-case-setting-run"
    assert !shell.remove_tree(scratch).is_err()
    assert !shell.mkdir_all(scratch + "/x.case/here").is_err()
    assert !write_file(path: scratch + "/x.case/here/kept", text: "").is_err()
    probe = variables_probe.built(scratch).must()
    root = repository_root(scratch).must()
    windows = shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
    dir = scratch + "/x.case"
    s = Setting(
        environment: ["CPATH=", "C_INCLUDE_PATH=a b", "PKG_CONFIG_PATH=pa:<root>/pb", "PATH=<root>/build/no-tools"],
        links: [],
        directory: ""
    )
    assert skip_here(s) == ""
    said = ran(
        scratch: scratch,
        program: probe,
        words: [probe, "CPATH", "C_INCLUDE_PATH", "PKG_CONFIG_PATH", "PATH"],
        dir: dir,
        s: s,
        root: root
    ).must()
    lines = strings.split_on(text: said.out, byte: 10)
    assert said.code == 0 && lines.len() == 6
    assert lines.slice(from: 1, to: 6) == ["CPATH []", "C_INCLUDE_PATH [a b]", "PKG_CONFIG_PATH [pa" + separator(windows) + "<root>/pb]", "PATH [<root>/build/no-tools]", ""]
    assert shell.env(name: "C_INCLUDE_PATH").must() != "a b"
    moved = Setting(environment: ["CPATH=<root>/inc", "C_INCLUDE_PATH=:"], links: [], directory: "here")

    if windows
        assert core_strings.contains(s: skip_here(moved), substr: "folder `here`")
    else
        assert skip_here(moved) == ""
        there = ran(
            scratch: scratch,
            program: probe,
            words: [probe, "CPATH", "C_INCLUDE_PATH"],
            dir: dir,
            s: moved,
            root: root
        ).must()
        assert there.code == 0 && there.out == "in <root>/" + dir + "/here\nCPATH [<root>/inc]\nC_INCLUDE_PATH [:]\n"
    assert !shell.remove_tree(scratch).is_err()
